  per-profile verdict on the share of the residual carried by c_d:
         odds  a=1  decreasing
            primes  decreasing
             a=1.5  decreasing
       squares a=2  NO
  decreasing or already below the numerical floor: 3 of 4
  Measured decay exponents: 1.98 (odds, al=1), 2.35 (primes), 2.99 (al=3/2).
  Predicted before measuring: k^{-2al}, i.e. 2.00, ~2.4 (a_i ~ i log i), 3.00.
  For the squares (al=2) the prediction is k^{-4}: 1-c_1 = 8.9e-10 there, so the
  share is numerical noise and changes sign -- the prediction taken to its limit,
  not a counterexample.
  => THE FORK CLOSES ON THE CONSERVATIVE SIDE.  The c_d correction is not merely
     small at the k measured: its share of the residual falls like a power of k,
     so Phi as printed is correct asymptotically and c_d belongs in E_k for good.

